      "claim": "In humans, the guanidine-rich compound mitoguazone showed limited CSF penetration (CSF/plasma 0.6–7%), directly demonstrating that guanidine-containing polar molecules can have poor CNS access; this supports fail for the dicationic guanidine query.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C09"],
      "claim": "A polar basic piperidine metabolite ([18F]FEP-4MOH) showed low rat brain uptake (<0.05% dose/g), indicating that polar basic amines can be BBB-impermeable; the query is even more polar and fully ionized, supporting fail.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C10"],
      "claim": "A lipophilic piperidine ether showed a rat brain/plasma ratio of 0.69 and was classified as permeable, providing high-transfer evidence that basic amines can cross the BBB; however, it lacks the guanidine and very low logD of the query, so it only weakly contradicts fail.",
      "evidence_role": "contradictory"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C02"],
      "claim": "Biperiden, a lipophilic piperidine anticholinergic, showed brain/plasma ratios of 7–12, strong evidence that basic amines can achieve high CNS exposure; but its lipophilic, non-guanidine structure is not representative of the query's dicationic state.",
      "evidence_role": "contradictory"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C07"],
      "claim": "Trihexyphenidyl, another lipophilic piperidine anticholinergic, penetrates the BBB easily by PET; this supports the general ability of basic amines to cross, but does not overcome the query's guanidine/ionization liability.",
      "evidence_role": "contradictory"
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "moderate",
  "decision_summary": "The query is guanethidine, a dicationic guanidine-azocane with logD -2.7 and zero neutral fraction at pH 7.4. Although several lipophilic basic amines in the evidence are CNS-penetrant, the direct guanidine-containing CSF evidence (C06) and polar basic metabolite brain-uptake evidence (C09) indicate that the guanidine/dicationic character is a decisive barrier. Meaningful CNS access after systemic administration is therefore unlikely.",
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct experimental brain/plasma or CSF measurement for guanethidine itself in the provided evidence.",
    "Transporter-mediated uptake/efflux (OCT, P-gp, BCRP) at the BBB is not experimentally characterized for the query.",
    "The high-transfer CNS-permeable analogues lack the guanidine and full ionization of the query, limiting their transferability."
  ],
